  "sourceLaws": [
    "Crop stride must be 32-byte aligned; invalid stride spins before engine initialization.",
    "Scale copies exactly fourteen coefficient words into lifetime-bound stack storage; input/output byte widths and strides shift right by one.",
    "Copy checks nonnull planes and eight-byte address alignment, input half-width alignment and height alignment after initialize and packet zeroing; invalid input spins.",
    "All four orchestrators publish current task before hardware begin, clear it after wait, complete cleanup on both event outcomes, and return one exactly when event bit0x20 is absent.",
    "Planes clone nullable descriptors into zero-filled locals; packed mode derives from flags0x10000 and0x10, except fifth ignores0x10000 and fourth always uses mode2.",
    "Planes auxiliary height ratio is third.height/fourth.height, admitted ratios2,4,8,16; zero fourth.height selects0; every other ratio spins.",
    "Geometry snapshot saturates record index12; timestamp then overlaps counter, and first register overlaps trailer. Crop snapshot saturates index24 and first register overlaps counter. Final counters increment the value present after record writes.",
    "Snapshot output pointers are reloaded before every register store. Geometry/crop snapshots do not guard a null pointer when enabled; processing snapshot does."
  ],
